  "solution": "Divide \\(x^3\\) by \\(x^2+5x+1\\):\n\n\\[\nx^3 = (x^2+5x+1)(x) -5x^2 - x\n\\]\n\nNow divide \\(-5x^2-x\\):\n\n\\[\n-5x^2-x = (x^2+5x+1)(-5) + 24x+5\n\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[\nx^3 = (x^2+5x+1)(x-5) + 24x+5\n\\]\n\nThus the remainder is \\(24x+5\\).\n\nThe answer is \\(24x+5\\).",
